  The shell's startup                                                           
  zsh is started the way a terminal starts it -- `zsh -i -c exit`, each start   
  bounded by 10 s -- so the number describes the start you wait through when    
  you open a terminal. The plan runs 5 such starts, and the median is the       
  middle one: not an average, and not a single run.                             
  What the press will measure: the interactive start, 5 runs, no warm-up        
  first, and no clean comparison is measured. [m] changes the start, [n] the    
  number of runs, [w] the warm-up, and [b] the clean comparison. That           
  … and 47 more                                                                 
                                                                                
